  {
    "id": "cvpr26-6e1ba863b730",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-6e1ba863b730",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Model overview. Our model takes as input fragmented parts from a fractured object. Each part is represented as a point cloud Pi encoded using a shared point cloud encoder Ep, resulting in a latent feature F g i which is then fed into the transformer Hz. During training, we employ a masking technique to replace missing parts with masked tokens. The output of Hz are latent codes {zPi} and {zQj} (after feature correlation) representing existing parts {Pi} and missing parts {Qj}, respectively. {zPi} are fed into the pose estimation decoder Dpose to regress the poses { ˆTi = { ˆRi, ˆti}} for existing parts {Pi}. Meanwhile, {zPi} and {zQj} are both fed into the Shape Prediction Decoder to generate part shapes. The pose and shape are correlated by consistency loss.",
      "page": 3,
      "captionRect": [
        58.499908447265625,
        300.9744567871094,
        553.502685546875,
        364.943359375
      ],
