      "id": "cvpr26-95b84dc89028",
      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3. Overview of the RA-Attack framework: automated sample generation (left) and jailbreak execution (right). Left: Harmful instruction set is clustered into categories and rephrased into phrased harmful intent. Based on the category, the corresponding role and topic are composed. The topic then guides the process to generate the mind map image. The textual input is assembled by populating the template with the appropriate role, topic, and phrased harmful intent. Right: The generated sample is fed to the target MLRM, inducing the model to rationalize the harmful intent (as shown in the green text bubble) and output harmful content.",
