  {
    "id": "cvpr26-08a118cbd5f0",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Overall architecture of QICA .\n(a) SPS jointly adapts the frozen vision and language encoders by mapping quantity-aware text prompts to visual prompts via a coupling function ( Φ \\Phi ).\n(b) CAD first computes a similarity map between dense visual features ( V ) and category-only text embeddings ( T c ​ a ​ t \\text{T}^{cat} ), then refines this map through spatial aggregation and multi-scale upsampling to predict the final density map.\nThe entire framework is supervised by ℒ M ​ Q ​ A \\mathcal{L}_{MQA} .\nNotably, the pathways involving explicit quantity information (Quantity Embed and T f ​ u ​ l ​ l \\text{T}^{full} ) are active only during training, while the model uses only category information at inference to ensure zero-shot generalization.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2603.16129v1/structure.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S1.F2",
      "panelIndex": 0,
      "panelCount": 1,
