      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. The IMPO framework, built on GRPO, generates image-level rewards. The old policy πθold produces candidate sequences, rendered and compared to the target to compute the Image Matching Score (IMS). The normalized IMS yields the advantage, used to update the policy πθ via a clipped surrogate loss. KL regularization constrains deviations from the πθref, enhancing training stability.",
