    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Overall framework of our method. (a) Predict Future: Given point clouds 𝒫 t \\mathcal{P}_{t} and 𝒫 t + k \\mathcal{P}_{t+k} , the online encoder f ϕ f_{\\phi} produces features 𝐳 t \\mathbf{z}_{t} and 𝐳 t + k \\mathbf{z}_{t+k} . The inverse dynamics model g ψ g_{\\psi} takes the difference ( 𝐳 t + k − 𝐳 t ) (\\mathbf{z}_{t+k}-\\mathbf{z}_{t}) to infer the latent action 𝜶 t → t + k \\boldsymbol{\\alpha}_{t\\rightarrow t+k} . The target encoder f ξ f_{\\xi} (EMA) encodes 𝒫 t + k \\mathcal{P}_{t+k} to obtain 𝐳 ~ t + k \\tilde{\\mathbf{z}}_{t+k} . The forward dynamics model h θ h_{\\theta} predicts ( 𝐳 t , 𝜶 t → t + k ) ↦ 𝐳 ^ t + k (\\mathbf{z}_{t},\\boldsymbol{\\alpha}_{t\\rightarrow t+k})\\mapsto\\hat{\\mathbf{z}}_{t+k} and aligns it with 𝐳 ~ t + k \\tilde{\\mathbf{z}}_{t+k} , guiding f ϕ f_{\\phi} to learn dynamics-aware representations. (b) Predict History: Using ( 𝐳 t − 𝐳 t + k ) (\\mathbf{z}_{t}-\\mathbf{z}_{t+k}) , g ψ g_{\\psi} infers 𝜶 t + k → t \\boldsymbol{\\alpha}_{t+k\\rightarrow t} . The encoder f ξ f_{\\xi} encodes 𝒫 t \\mathcal{P}_{t} to obtain 𝐳 ~ t \\tilde{\\mathbf{z}}_{t} , while h θ h_{\\theta} predicts ( 𝐳 t + k , 𝜶 t + k → t ) ↦ 𝐳 ^ t (\\mathbf{z}_{t+k},\\boldsymbol{\\alpha}_{t+k\\rightarrow t})\\mapsto\\hat{\\mathbf{z}}_{t} aligned with 𝐳 ~ t \\tilde{\\mathbf{z}}_{t} . Other steps are symmetric to (a). (c) Notation overview.",
