  {
    "id": "cvpr26-fd3cbd45946b",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-fd3cbd45946b",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. The pipeline of our proposed dynamic important example mining (DIEM). Compared with the vanilla RFT pipeline, our DIEM introduces only two lightweight steps: (1) Dynamic Data Importance Measuring, which evaluates the importance of each sample within the current batch using our proposed influence estimator in Eq.4; and (2) Dynamic Data Reweighting, which reallocates sample weights based on their importance. The reweighting step is formulated as a constrained optimization problem that preserves the overall gradient magnitude while emphasizing the most important samples (defined in Eq.6, and we further provide an efficient closed-form solution in Eq.7. Overall, DIEM is highly efficient, intuitive, and broadly compatible with existing RFT algorithms [15, 38–40].",
      "page": 2,
      "captionRect": [
