    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3 : (a) Overview of the proposed ComPose framework, which supports both RGB-D and depth-only settings, where the latter omits the RGB images 𝑰 rgb {\\bm{I}}^{\\mathrm{rgb}} . (b) The initial coarse keypoints 𝑪 kpt {\\bm{C}}^{\\mathrm{kpt}} are adaptively selected from missing and visible candidates { 𝑪 miss , 𝑪 vis } \\{{\\bm{C}}^{\\mathrm{miss}},{\\bm{C}}^{\\mathrm{vis}}\\} . These coarse keypoints are then progressively refined through feature interactions with the partial features 𝑭 part {\\bm{F}}^{\\mathrm{part}} to recover complete object geometries, including refined keypoints 𝑷 kpt {\\bm{P}}^{\\mathrm{kpt}} and dense shapes 𝑷 com {\\bm{P}}^{\\mathrm{com}} . (c) The keypoint features 𝑭 kpt {\\bm{F}}^{\\mathrm{kpt}} are enhanced into 𝑭 geo {\\bm{F}}^{\\mathrm{geo}} via geometric relation encoding, incorporating both local and global geometric context { 𝑬 l , 𝑬 g } \\{{\\bm{E}}^{\\mathrm{l}},{\\bm{E}}^{\\mathrm{g}}\\} . To ensure robust coordinate transformations, the pairwise geometric relations 𝑮 {\\bm{G}} among keypoints are constrained to maintain alignment between the observation and canonical spaces.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2605.25553v1/method.png",
