      "figure": "Figure 4",
      "caption": "Figure 4 : Overall framework of IQPIR. (a) In the codebook learning stage, a dual-codebook architecture is proposed. The HQ+ codebook is learned to quantize Z h Z_{h} only when the quality score of x h x_{h} is higher than the threshold S t ​ h ​ r S_{thr} .\n(b) In the codebook lookup stage, we input the quality score S S as a condition into Transformer T , which predicts two code sequences at the same time.\nThe two codebooks are leveraged to look up the corresponding code entries. Finally, the NR-IQA model is utilized to calculate the quality loss ℒ q ​ u ​ a ​ l ​ i ​ t ​ y \\mathcal{L}_{quality} .",
