    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Overview of TrackMAE. In the lower branch, a video clip 𝐕 \\mathbf{V} is first patchified and masked. The visible tokens are fed to a ViT encoder Φ \\Phi . Then the decoder Ψ s ​ p ​ a ​ t ​ i ​ a ​ l \\Psi_{spatial} aims to reconstruct spatial features based on the encoder output. In the upper branch, the input video clip is processed by a CoTracker3 module, extracting sparse point trajectories. The encoder output is then passed to a second decoder Ψ M ​ o ​ t ​ i ​ o ​ n \\Psi_{Motion} , which aims to predict the extracted trajectories. The training objective combines both motion and spatial reconstruction.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2603.27268v1/main_copy_v2.png",
