      "id": "cvpr26-f0f764cfc460",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of BiGMINT: A biologically guided multimodal framework integrating HCI, protein sequence, and compound SMILES for compound activity prediction (a). A chemoproteomics model (c) and a foundation model (d) are used to extract molecular interaction and phenotypic signals respectively. The molecular signal then guides the aggregation of the phenotypic features in (e), which is then fused with the molecular signal in (f). PPI is used as a prior in (g) to enrich task-specific features for compound activity prediction (h).",
