    "id": "cvpr26-d7b17ec33d08",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-d7b17ec33d08",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Overview of BA-GS. Our method follows the classical Gaussian Splatting pipeline but introduces a Bayesian optimization stage that adaptively refines the Gaussian primitives based on uncertainty estimation. The process consists of the following steps: (1) Initialize 3D Gaussians from a pretrained reconstruction. (2) Fit a VB-GMM to capture the latent spatial and color distribution for improved initialization and coverage. (3) Treat per-primitive updates as noisy observations and apply uncertainty-aware filtering to balance estimation and observation confidence. Iterate until convergence to obtain a stable, regularized, and noise-suppressed Gaussian representation.",
      "page": 2,
      "captionRect": [
        58.5,
        324.718994140625,
        553.4990234375,
        377.5213623046875
      ],
      "score": 41,
