    "id": "cvpr26-14d90c7593df",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-14d90c7593df",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Architecture designed based on the human reasoning loop. (a) Architecture and Reasoning Loop: The model comprises UM and SM, both utilizing recurrent Transformer blocks. Through multiple interactions between UM and SM, the model continuously updates the rule representation ˜ei,t−1 and the solution state Zi,t to progressively optimize the prediction ˆyi,t. (b) Rule-Embedding Isomorphism: Illustrates how the UM maps example pairs into a feature space. Examples sharing the same transformation rule (ei,1, ei,2 from task i) are clustered closely together, while those with different rules (ej,1) are pushed apart, defining a specific “Halting region” for task i. (c) Adaptive Reasoning Halting: The generated draft solution from SM is fed back into UM. If its rule representation ei,ans falls within the halting region, the reasoning loop terminates to output the final result; otherwise, it proceeds to the next reasoning loop.",
      "page": 4,
      "captionRect": [
