      "id": "cvpr26-a168064ee0df",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. The pipeline of DrivePI consists of the following steps. First, we employ a vision encoder to extract features from images and LiDAR data, obtaining latent BEV features that are then converted into vision tokens by a spatial projector. Next, we feed both vision tokens and text tokens into the MLLM to generate output tokens. The MLLM produces responses through four specialized heads: a text head for scene understanding in an auto-regressive manner, a 3D occupancy head for accurate spatial perception, an occupancy ﬂow head for pixel-level motion prediction, and an action diffusion head for trajectory planning.",
      "page": 3,
      "captionRect": [
